## STEP 1: Master build prompt (paste into a NEW Google AI Studio build)

```
Build "Calmly" from scratch: a two-sided appointment product for a private nutritionist (admin side) and her clients (client side) sharing ONE Supabase database. Stack: Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 + react-router-dom + lucide-react. This is an internship assignment, so prioritise reliability, clarity and honesty over novelty. If anything cannot be done, say so plainly at the end.

## 1. MOBILE RULES (non-negotiable)
- index.html has <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">.
- No horizontal scroll at 360px. Containers use w-full / max-w-* / flex / grid, never fixed pixel widths.
- Every input, select and textarea uses font-size >= 16px (stops mobile auto-zoom). Tap targets >= 44px.
- Use 100dvh not 100vh; bottom tab bar respects env(safe-area-inset-bottom).
- Must be fully usable on a phone with NO pinching or zooming. Check at 360, 390, 768, 1280px.

## 2. DATABASE (already exists; NEVER create, alter or drop tables from app code)
appointments(id uuid, client_name, phone text null, date date, time time, status in ('Booked','Done','No-show','Cancelled'), source in ('client','nutritionist','seed'), notes, confirmed_at timestamptz, reason text, visit_type text default 'In clinic', seed_key text unique-when-not-null, created_at, updated_at).
waitlist(id, client_name, phone, date, notified, created_at). audit_log(id, appointment_id, action, old_status, new_status, details, changed_at) is READ-ONLY for the app.
The database enforces: partial unique index on (date,time) where status <> 'Cancelled' (no double booking), phone format ^[6-9][0-9]{9}$, name length 2-80, 30-minute grid 09:00-17:30, and for source='client' rows: no past slots, max 60 days ahead, max 3 upcoming Booked per phone. RLS has NO delete policy, so the app must NEVER call delete. Cancel = update status to 'Cancelled'.
Map database errors to friendly messages: code 23505 -> "That slot was just taken, please pick another" (then refresh slots); code 23514 -> a field validation message; any error text containing "past", "60 days" or "Maximum 3" -> show that text kindly; network/other -> "Something went wrong, please try again" with a Retry button. Never show raw SQL errors to users, but log them to the console.

## 3. CONFIG AND SECRETS
Read VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY from import.meta.env only; never hardcode keys. Sanitise: trim whitespace and quotes; strip a leading "VITE_SUPABASE_URL=" or "VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=" prefix; strip trailing slash and /rest/v1. URL must start with https:// and end with .supabase.co. REFUSE any key starting "sb_secret" or containing "service_role" with a red error ("Secret key detected, use the publishable key"). If config is invalid or missing, show a clear red banner naming the exact variable and problem, and run in a LocalStorage demo mode with a visible, permanent "Demo mode: data stays on this device" banner. Never switch to demo mode silently. Add .gitignore (node_modules, dist, .env, .env.local) and .env.example with placeholder values. Never print a full key anywhere.

## 4. DATA ACCESS
One repository interface (SupabaseRepo plus LocalStorageRepo). UI components never call Supabase directly. Realtime subscription on appointments, with 5-second polling as fallback; show a small "Live" indicator. Every write: disable the button while saving (no double submit), show success or error toast. Updates from admin send the last-seen updated_at as a condition (optimistic concurrency); if 0 rows change, show "This appointment was changed elsewhere, reloaded" and refetch.

## 5. NORMALISERS (src/lib/normalize.ts, pure functions, unit tested)
parseDate: DD/MM/YYYY, D/M/YYYY, DD-MM-YYYY, YYYY-MM-DD (day-first), reject impossible dates like 31/02/2026. parseTime: "10:00", "14:00", "11:30am", "4 pm", "4PM", "12 am" (00:00), "12 pm" (12:00) -> HH:mm 24h; reject garbage. normalizePhone: strip spaces, dashes, brackets, +91, leading 0; require 10 digits starting 6-9; display as "98200 11111". Client key = phone, else lower-cased name.

